Title: blackbox: concurrent erg new race window
Created: 2026-05-30
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-30T07:04Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context

This is a confirmed bug. Reproduced 2026-05-30:

```
$ for i in 1..8 do (erg new "Worker $i task" DIR &) done
CREATED 0001-worker-1-task.erg
CREATED 0001-worker-2-task.erg
...  (all 8 succeed)
$ erg check DIR
ERG CHECK FAILED: duplicate ID '0001' in 8 files
```

`erg new` uses `nextID()` (reads max existing ID + 1) then `createExclusive()` (O_EXCL write).
`O_EXCL` prevents clobbering the exact same path, but **different titles produce different slugs
and therefore different paths** — all 8 succeed, all named `0001-worker-N-task.erg`. The
duplicate-ID detection is in `erg check`, not in `erg new`. After the race the store is silently
broken until someone runs `check`.

The harness spawns parallel agents that each create tickets — this is the exact failure mode.

## Root cause

`nextID()` is a pure read (max+1). Two concurrent readers see the same max (or an empty store)
and both compute `0001`. `createExclusive`'s O_EXCL is keyed on the full path including slug, not
on the 4-digit NNNN prefix. So same-ID-different-slug bypasses the guard entirely.

## Fix

Optimistic post-check, consistent with erg's stateless and optimistic design:

After `createExclusive` succeeds, glob for `NNNN-*.erg` in the store. If more than one file
matches, delete the just-created file and retry — `cmdNew` calls `nextID` again and attempts
the next free slot. No lock files, no claim artifacts, no serialization. Collisions are detected
after the fact and retried, the same way git handles concurrent operations.

Claim files and store locks are ruled out: both introduce side-state that violates the stateless
contract.

## Implementation notes (plan phase)

- Add to `tests/test_new.sh` — not a new file (avoids Makefile TEST_SUITES coupling)
- `CDIR=$(mktemp -d)` **outside the repo**: if inside the worktree, `nextID` Pass 2/3
  scans sibling worktrees and injects existing IDs, breaking the assertions
- `maxAttempts = 20` hard cap; emit a loud error on exhaustion rather than hanging
- Update stale comment at `test_new.sh` line 107: "O_EXCL guards against concurrent
  races (untestable sequentially)" — contradicted by the new test
- Run `make docs` after changing `helpNew` and `createExclusive` godoc: `test_docs.sh`
  gates on `docs/erg-manual.md` freshness and will fail if stale
- `path/filepath` and `os` already imported in `new.go` — no import block changes needed
- Verify test red-fails against the bug-present binary before applying the fix

## Implementation notes (from imagine phase)

- Only `cmdNew` in `new.go` changes. `nextid.go`, `createExclusive`, `slugify`,
  `resolveAuthor` are unchanged.
- `resolveAuthor()` stays outside the loop — author is constant across retries.
  Only `id`, `filename`, `path`, and `content` (which embeds the timestamp)
  recompute per iteration.
- With the fix, all N invocations succeed — each retries until it wins a unique
  slot. The test should assert all 10 produce CREATED, not just "some."
- No glob into `closed/` needed — `erg new` only writes to the top-level store.
- Do not extract a helper; inline the 10-line loop in `cmdNew`.
- Do not add jitter or backoff — the ID space is linear, each retry calls
  `nextID` fresh.
- "Test marked integration" means the test lives in the shell integration suite
  (`tests/`) and spawns background jobs — there is no formal marker system for
  shell tests.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `test_new.sh` (or `test_concurrent_new.sh`): N=10 parallel `erg new` with distinct titles,
      sync barrier via named pipe → all 10 produce `CREATED`, all 10 NNNN prefixes are distinct,
      `erg check` exits 0
- [ ] Negative control: N=10 sequential `erg new` → all 10 succeed with distinct IDs (proves the
      assertion is not vacuously true)
- [ ] `make check` passes after the fix

